cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Vox2SegLAM: joint subcortical segmentation and anatomical landmark detection on brain MRI"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rekik
    given-names: Ahmed
    email: ahmed.rekik.1@ens.etsmtl.ca
    affiliation: "École de Technologie Supérieure"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-9369-857X"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-06"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Neuro-iX/Vox2SegLAM"
url: "https://github.com/Neuro-iX/Vox2SegLAM"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24205672"
abstract: >-
  Vox2SegLAM predicts subcortical structures and anatomical landmarks from a T1-weighted
  brain MRI in a single forward pass. A residual U-Net produces the features; a graph
  network refines landmark coordinates over a landmark graph and a local patch head adds
  a sub-voxel correction. The anatomical protocol that places a structure boundary on a
  landmark plane is written in a small declarative language and can be enforced on the
  predicted segmentation.
keywords:
  - neuroimaging
  - magnetic resonance imaging
  - image segmentation
  - landmark detection
  - graph neural network
  - subcortical structures
